1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,449
01 · Frame Studio
Real local application. Silent walkthrough with chapter captions; no paid API calls.

2
00:00:06,449 --> 00:00:10,994
02 · Storyboard and templates
Select, add and reorder editable scenes; JSON remains the production document.

3
00:00:10,994 --> 00:00:28,103
03 · Typography and canvas editing
Type directly, choose offline fonts, move and resize elements, then undo and redo.

4
00:00:28,103 --> 00:00:50,467
04 · Shapes and vector library
Native editable shapes and 18 original vector symbols; not generated photographs.

5
00:00:50,467 --> 00:01:06,573
05 · Supplied images
Import a local PNG; cover crops centrally and contain preserves the whole asset.

6
00:01:06,573 --> 00:01:37,820
06 · Charts and verified data
Edit real labels and values, then switch among six chart types.

7
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:57,036
07 · Animated data story
Load a purpose-built authored demo, then inspect line tracing, slice filling and typography.

8
00:01:57,036 --> 00:02:19,962
08 · Element motion and pacing
Four coordinated motion characters, individual easing, intensity, start and duration.

9
00:02:19,962 --> 00:02:41,219
09 · Full project playback
One master clock, scene transitions, pause/resume, speed and backwards scrubbing.

10
00:02:41,219 --> 00:03:01,912
10 · Paths, groups and semantic chunks
Advanced JSON tracks are validated; grouped motion and reveals share preview/export timing.

11
00:03:01,912 --> 00:03:18,868
11 · Backgrounds, notes and aspect ratios
Choose scene treatment, narration notes and portrait/square/landscape output.

12
00:03:18,868 --> 00:03:55,997
12 · Local AI generation
Actual offline Qwen generation: grounded content, art direction and timed-shot planning.

13
00:03:55,997 --> 00:04:12,664
13 · Hosted generation and optional stages
Controls only: provider configuration, disclosure, images, vision critique and one bounded repair. No API call submitted.

14
00:04:12,664 --> 00:04:48,417
14 · Exports and narration safeguards
Actually export a static editable deck and silent MP4. Hosted narration requires separate configuration and consent.

15
00:04:48,417 --> 00:04:59,892
15 · Regeneration, persistence and mobile
Hosted shot regeneration requires a configured provider; JSON export preserves the project. Mobile controls use the same editor.

16
00:04:59,892 --> 00:05:04,608
16 · Walkthrough complete
Local features and real exports shown. Cloud generation, image generation and narration need separate live verification.
